<p>Would love to give feedback, but there's nothing here to give feedback on. Sure, you have a teen, a duck, and their mutually exclusive viruses, but we have no idea why the teen or the duck are important to the story, and no idea what the viruses do.</p>
<p>That said: Your Central Narrative should go on the page type; this is usually the space where you go into the details of how your SCP works and its story. &quot;Interesting Layout&quot; is not a hook unless you have a truly interesting layout; this is why we should care about the SCP and/or how it fits into the universe as a whole.</p>
<p>I'd love to give you some feedback, but there is just nothing to give feedback on.</p>

