<p>1) It's a bad sign when you're actually asking for suggestions on how to fill more space&#8230;Also, you don't need to mention how many green lights you need.</p>
<p>2) The hook is actually fine; it's fine to have a whimsical SCP in there every so often, but you may want to build that up a little more. Also, you can truncate most of the elevator pitch; just &quot;How can a hot-air balloon do this?&quot; is fine, although adding a little more as to its purpose would help.</p>
<p>3) The Central Narrative is your biggest problem. Not only do you have some grammatical issues that need to be worked on, but you're also lacking any kind of history with this guy. You need some sort of story, as well as who he would be on the defensive against. You have a hot-air balloon doing a lot of weirdness; there has to be some sort of origin story there. Figure out what it is.</p>

