<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A pond that become active in the winter by becoming frozen. When the pond becomes frozen, ice statues that take the appearance of Templar Knights will form and as a result, people who enter the SCP will be sent into a syndrome like state where they are commit acts of violence towards certain places.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> This takes place in December of 1993 in the woods of Alaska. The SCP Foundation was alerted to a location after strange reports of people worshipping the statues or disappearances relating to them started to become noticed.</p>
<p>As a result, the SCP Foundation attempts to investigate the anomaly and apprehend the cultists by sending four Foundation soldiers but as a result, the soldiers that were sent to the location return back to the Foundation Site attacking the scientists within the site in order to release the other SCPs within it. Of course, this fails and the incident results in the Foundation to be on high alert of the pond and result in them using a Mobile Task Force unit in order to investigate and contain the SCP.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The anomaly causes the person who encountered the pond and the statues to be stuck in a trance where they believe that have to do a certain trial or mission to fight for the religious cause. This would be attacking organizations, individuals, locations, etc., that would be considered against their faith.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I don’t know too much on the MTF but from reading the requirements on the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">Mobile Task Force</a> article, any user can use an existing MTF for their story if I remember correctly. Of course, you can correct me if I am wrong.</p>

