<p>You're really going to have to expand on this concept a lot more before I can offer really any useful feedback here.</p>
<p>Like, how are the trio related? Why are they being treated as a single SCP object instead of three unrelated ones? How does it tie into 'two ideas they can't get out of their head' and the what's the actual story you're telling here? What is the 'social interaction between the anomalies'? What events do they react to? How does this all come together to tell a compelling, cohesive story?</p>
<p>My concern is it sounds like a lot of this is backstory; and I generally don't vibe with that in a concept. My other concern is that you don't mention the Foundation at all in the pitch: the Foundation write the SCP article and hence are your POV characters, and so you need to like&#8230;have them actually take a protagonistic role in your story usually since everything has to be from their perspective.</p>

